{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"question":"CipherDoc final snapshot 2026-09-22 v1.0.0 release gates ship readiness open blockers","page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-08\\n\\n# Slack Thread: API Authentication Deferral\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:07] Bob**: Looking into REST API auth for v1.0. Do we need a full auth story now, or is trusted local network enough for the first release?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 13:22] Diana**: Given the PII involved, something robust would be nice. But if this is strictly local-network-only, we might not need it for v1.0.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 14:00] Bob**: Doing a short study either way — what we'd need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-29 14:23] Diana**: If we defer, we should at least write down the v1.1 requirements so we don't lose them.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:01] Alice**: Team, we're falling behind on core engine work. I'm deferring the auth module to v1.1. For v1.0, the API assumes a trusted local network.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:19] Diana**: Manageable if we stay local-network-only. I'll note the deferral.\\n\\n**[2026-06-30 09:21] Bob**: Fine. I'll keep the seams clean so adding auth later isn't a rewrite.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:04] Bob**: Still deferred — capturing v1.1 auth requirements while we remember them: REST auth with rotation support, since v1.0 is local-network-only.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 11:06] Diana**: Agreed. Folding that into the deferred-work notes so it survives until v1.1 planning.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 10:11] Alice**: Rechecked release scope for v1.0 — auth stays deferred to post-v1.0.0. Trusted-network assumption still holds.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 08 slack thread api authent deferr channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 08 20 2026 06 28 13 07 bob look into rest api auth for v1 0 do we need a full auth stori now or is trust local network enough for the first releas 2026 06 28 13 22 diana given the pii involv someth robust would be nice but if this is strict local network onli we might not need it for v1 0 2026 06 28 14 00 bob do a short studi either way what we d need if we keep auth in scope versus what we defer 2026 06 29 14 23 diana if we defer we should at least write down the v1 1 requir so we don t lose them 2026 06 30 09 01 alic team we re fall behind on core engin work i m defer the auth modul to v1 1 for v1 0 the api assum a trust local network 2026 06 30 09 19 diana manag if we stay local network onli i ll note the deferr 2026 06 30 09 21 bob fine i ll keep the seam clean so ad auth later isn t a rewrit 2026 08 0511 04 bob still defer captur v1 1 auth requir while we rememb them rest auth with rotat support sinc v1 0 is local network onli 2026 08 0511 06 diana agre fold that into the defer work note so it surviv until v1 1 plan 2026 08 20 10 11 alic recheck releas scope for v1 0 auth stay defer to post v1 0 0 trust network assumpt still hold\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f690d68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"id\": \"8320be9e419ec3ba\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.37286374583764137, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.22524642119663058, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71730417, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f690d68a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-defer-auth.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1525, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:17\", \"token_count\": 479, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-58\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Upstream Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Diana**: Bad news on the high-DPI rendering fix. The rotation fix Charlie pushed works for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix charli push work for simpl case but it s complet break on document with nest form xobject 2026 09 1010 43 charli yeah i look into it the under render librari we re use pdf lib core ha a known bug in how it handl coordin for xobject when a parent transform is appli 2026 09 1010 55 alic can we patch it 2026 09 1010 56 charli no 2026 09 10 11 35 charli it s deep in their c core i ve open an issu with the upstream maintain but they haven t respond 2026 09 10 11 37 evan we can t wait for an upstream fix if we re hit the releas gate can we work around it by flatten the pdfs first 2026 09 10 11 51 charli flatten might work but it ll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layer 2026 09 10 12 29 alic diana charli let s leav high dpi render block for now we need to decid if we can ship with this limit or if we need a differ render librari entir 2026 09 10 12 32 diana agre it onli affect a small subset of complex document but we should document it a a known issu\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"id\": \"72425f09d11fcc84\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3577462345690132, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.188852120812876, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7518325, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9310f048a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-10-high-dpi-upstream-block.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1371, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:29\", \"token_count\": 414, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-21\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-21\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-21\\n\\n**Title**: Release v1.0 Gates\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-07-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTrack the mandatory release gates for CipherDoc v1.0 (WS-03). The initial checklist draft depended on T001 through T006 and T010. A later prerequisite audit found the checklist still incomplete while T005 (Docker image slim-down/CVE work) and T029 (Windows code-signing) remained open, and release notes were drafted in parallel while gates stayed open. Diana placed a security-gate hold on the release pending both T005's Docker slim-down/CVE work and T029's Windows Defender/SmartScreen code-signing; the task remains Active with those two gates unresolved.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-21\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-21\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-21\\n\\n**Title**: Release v1.0 Gates\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-07-08\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Checklist dependencies T001-T006 and T010 satisfied (met; those tasks are Completed).\\n\\n- T005 (Docker image size/CVE) and T029 (Windows code-signing) gates clear (not yet met; task remains Active pending both).\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-21\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-21\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-21\\n\\n**Title**: Release v1.0 Gates\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-07-08\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTrack the mandatory release gates for CipherDoc v1.0 (WS-03). The initial checklist draft depended on T001 through T006 and T010. A later prerequisite audit found the checklist still incomplete while T005 (Docker image slim-down/CVE work) and T029 (Windows code-signing) remained open, and release notes were drafted in parallel while gates stayed open. Diana placed a security-gate hold on the release pending both T005's Docker slim-down/CVE work and T029's Windows Defender/SmartScreen code-signing; the task remains Active with those two gates unresolved.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 21 sourc id src cu ciph 21 task id ciph 21 titl releas v1 0 gate status activ assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 07 08 descript track the mandatori releas gate for cipherdoc v1 0 w 03 the initi checklist draft depend on t001 through t006 and t010 a later prerequisit audit found the checklist still incomplet while t005 docker imag slim down cve work and t029 window code sign remain open and releas note were draft in parallel while gate stay open diana place a secur gate hold on the releas pend both t005 s docker slim down cve work and t029 s window defend smartscreen code sign the task remain activ with those two gate unresolv clickup task ciph 21 sourc id src cu ciph 21 task id ciph 21 titl releas v1 0 gate status activ assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 07 08 accept criterion checklist depend t001 t006 and t010 satisfi met those task are complet t005 docker imag size cve and t029 window code sign gate clear not yet met task remain activ pend both clickup task ciph 21 sourc id src cu ciph 21 task id ciph 21 titl releas v1 0 gate status activ assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 07 08 descript track the mandatori releas gate for cipherdoc v1 0 w 03 the initi checklist draft depend on t001 through t006 and t010 a later prerequisit audit found the checklist still incomplet while t005 docker imag slim down cve work and t029 window code sign remain open and releas note were draft in parallel while gate stay open diana place a secur gate hold on the releas pend both t005 s docker slim down cve work and t029 s window defend smartscreen code sign the task remain activ with those two gate unresolv\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e97842848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"id\": \"d0ddf0dd50f07774\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34974335158854697, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1627904665550671, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78596675, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e97842848a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-21-Release-v1-Gates.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1139, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:27\", \"token_count\": 635, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34756612477756044, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18905293682508645, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71743023, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"be17298264309b61\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3470105692435568, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17072029606222397, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75835454, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-05\\n\\n# Release Checklist — v1.0 Gate Status (Draft)\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2005\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-12\\n\\nDraft checklist for T011 (Release v1.0 Gates). Per the task's own dependency list, this draft depends on T001 through T006 and T010.\\n\\n## Gate Status as of Today\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-05\\n\\n# Release Checklist — v1.0 Gate Status (Draft)\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2005\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-12\\n\\nDraft checklist for T011 (Release v1.0 Gates). Per the task's own dependency list, this draft depends on T001 through T006 and T010.\\n\\n## Blocking Item\\n\\nT005 is the only unmet dependency: the Docker image failed Diana's size/CVE review and was reopened on 2026-06-25. This checklist cannot close until that gate clears.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-05\\n\\n# Release Checklist — v1.0 Gate Status (Draft)\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2005\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-12\\n\\nDraft checklist for T011 (Release v1.0 Gates). Per the task's own dependency list, this draft depends on T001 through T006 and T010.\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nActive (Draft). Six of seven dependency gates are met; T005 remains open.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 05 releas checklist v1 0 gate status draft owner evan document key doc 2005 last updat 2026 07 12 draft checklist for t011 releas v1 0 gate per the task s own depend list this draft depend on t001 through t006 and t010 gate status a of today sourc id src gdoc 05 releas checklist v1 0 gate status draft owner evan document key doc 2005 last updat 2026 07 12 draft checklist for t011 releas v1 0 gate per the task s own depend list this draft depend on t001 through t006 and t010 block item t005 is the onli unmet depend the docker imag fail diana s size cve review and wa reopen on 2026 06 25 this checklist can not close until that gate clear sourc id src gdoc 05 releas checklist v1 0 gate status draft owner evan document key doc 2005 last updat 2026 07 12 draft checklist for t011 releas v1 0 gate per the task s own depend list this draft depend on t001 through t006 and t010 status activ draft six of seven depend gate are met t005 remain open\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9b23eee8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"id\": \"8bf53f4b1ae56706\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3410380683715761, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1507025833879658, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7851542, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9b23eee8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1077, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:40\", \"token_count\": 704, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Background: Path Fix Cleared Packaging\\n\\nBackslash path-handling defects that previously broke Windows builds were fixed on 2026-08-10, and a Windows build artifact was successfully produced by 2026-08-12. Packaging itself is no longer the blocker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Current Blocker: Missing Code-Signing Certificate\\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate procurement is the sole open blocker.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 background path fix clear packag backslash path handl defect that previous broke window build were fix on 2026 08 10 and a window build artifact wa success produc by 2026 08 12 packag itself is no longer the blocker sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 current blocker miss code sign certif the produc build artifact is unsign which trigger a smartscreen warn and defend flag the binari a untrust impact site it polici common block execut of unsign smartscreen flag binari outright which would prevent instal on target deploy workstat without a manual secur polici overrid root caus no code sign certif ha been procur or configur in the window build pipelin yet sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 path to resolut procur a code sign certif and wire sign into the releas build step is the onli remain item befor this clear the t029 window compat gate and by extens the t011 releas checklist which is hold on this exact sign gap alongsid the t005 imag slim down audit status activ build produc success sign certif procur is the sole open blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"7d9dbdfb5b6d7c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34076277524355675, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17072029606222397, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73752856, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1340, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 387, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-06\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Docker Image Size Optimization\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-08-12\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-25 09:35] Diana**: @Evan, I just pulled the latest `cipherdoc` image. It's 2.1GB! That's way too big for a local runtime deployment. Reopening the Docker packaging task.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 09:30] Evan**: Whoa, 2.1GB, and we still haven't closed out the CVE verification either. Looks like the full Ubuntu base is a big part of the bloat. I'll put together a multi-stage build plan targeting somewhere around 450MB.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 09:33] Diana**: That'd get it onto standard dev laptops without eating all the disk space. Let's aim for that.\\n\\n**[2026-08-01 10:04] Evan**: Multi-stage build plan is in place. Stripping out the build-time dependencies from the final artifact.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 13:11] Evan**: The multi-stage split alone still leaves the base layer too large. Swapping from `ubuntu:22.04` to `alpine:latest` as the base. Had some issues with `glibc` vs `musl`, but `gcompat` seems to fix it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-07 15:21] Evan**: Alpine swap didn't get us all the way there either. Just removed the unused OCR and runtime packages we aren't shipping in this build.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:00] Diana**: Checked the size and ran the CVE scan. We're still over the ~450MB target, and the CVE verification is still failing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:10] Evan**: Yeah, not where we need to be yet. There's still fluff in the Python site-packages layer, and I need to chase down what's tripping the CVE scan.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:13] Diana**: Reopened status stands until both the size and the CVE check are clean. I'll keep tracking it against the release checklist.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 06 slack thread docker imag size optim channel releas thread open 2026 06 25 last activ 2026 08 12 2026 06 25 09 35 diana evan i just pull the latest cipherdoc imag it s2 1gb that s way too big for a local runtim deploy reopen the docker packag task 2026 0801 09 30 evan whoa 2 1gb and we still haven t close out the cve verif either look like the full ubuntu base is a big part of the bloat i ll put togeth a multi stage build plan target somewher around 450mb 2026 0801 09 33 diana that d get it onto standard dev laptop without eat all the disk space let s aim for that 2026 0801 1004 evan multi stage build plan is in place strip out the build time depend from the final artifact 2026 08 04 13 11 evan the multi stage split alon still leaf the base layer too larg swap from ubuntu 22 04 to alpin latest a the base had some issu with glibc v musl but gcompat seem to fix it 2026 08 07 15 21 evan alpin swap didn t get u all the way there either just remov the unus ocr and runtim packag we aren t ship in this build 2026 08 12 09 00 diana check the size and ran the cve scan we re still over the 450mb target and the cve verif is still fail 2026 08 12 09 10 evan yeah not where we need to be yet there s still fluff in the python site packag layer and i need to chase down what s trip the cve scan 2026 08 12 09 13 diana reopen status stand until both the size and the cve check are clean i ll keep track it against the releas checklist\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8ee6a5a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-25-docker-size.md\", \"id\": \"87fb525087edc8d4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3387763723077346, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1785799604396209, \"vector_similarity\": 0.712568, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-25-docker-size.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8ee6a5a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-25-docker-size.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-25-docker-size.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1720, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:24\", \"token_count\": 513, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-07\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Blocked on Upstream PDF Library\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-26\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:10] Charlie**: Bad news on the offset mismatch fix. It's definitely coming from `pdfminer.six`. There's an open issue on their repo for the whitespace handling we're hitting.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:57] Alice**: Any workaround? We can't stay blocked on this forever.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:58] Charlie**: Leaving it blocked for now. Local patches aren't getting us a clean fix — it's too deep in the parser.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 14:18] Charlie**: Still watching upstream — there's a PR against pdfminer.six, #992, that should cover the whitespace fix, but it hasn't merged. No movement from the maintainers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 15:58] Charlie**: Spent some time this week evaluating whether we fork pdfminer.six ourselves to get the fix in sooner.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 16:01] Alice**: What's the team's read on that?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 17:55] Charlie**: We're passing on it. Maintaining a PDF parsing fork long-term is more risk than the wait. Staying blocked on #992.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:24] Charlie**: Checked again — #992 is still unmerged. No safe local path that doesn't involve owning a fork, so we're leaving the offset fix blocked pending the upstream merge.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Alice**: This is becoming a real risk for the v1.0 timeline.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Charlie**: Agreed, but I'd rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can't maintain.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 07 slack thread block on upstream pdf librari channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 26 last activ 2026 09 10 2026 06 26 09 10 charli bad news on the offset mismatch fix it s definit come from pdfminer six there s an open issu on their repo for the whitespac handl we re hit 2026 06 26 09 57 alic ani workaround we can t stay block on this forev 2026 06 26 09 58 charli leav it block for now local patch aren t get u a clean fix it s too deep in the parser 2026 08 05 14 18 charli still watch upstream there s a pr against pdfminer six 992 that should cover the whitespac fix but it hasn t merg no movement from the maintain 2026 08 20 15 58 charli spent some time this week evalu whether we fork pdfminer six ourselv to get the fix in sooner 2026 08 2016 01 alic what s the team s read on that 2026 08 2017 55 charli we re pass on it maintain a pdf pars fork long term is more risk than the wait stay block on 992 2026 09 1010 24 charli check again 992 is still unmerg no safe local path that doesn t involv own a fork so we re leav the offset fix block pend the upstream merg 2026 09 1010 41 alic this is becom a real risk for the v1 0 timelin 2026 09 1010 55 charli agre but i d rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can t maintain\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"id\": \"68389a2a4ecca69d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3365938877851775, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15803563969311077, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7532298, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1522, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:33\", \"token_count\": 462, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"7c000945298cb210\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33511741844018733, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1659654692002676, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7298053, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size