v1 0 gate per the task s own depend list this draft depend on t001 through t006 and t010 block item t005 is the onli unmet depend the docker imag fail diana s size cve review and wa reopen on 2026 06 25 this checklist can not close until that gate clear sourc id src gdoc 05 releas checklist v1 0 gate status draft owner evan document key doc 2005 last updat 2026 07 12 draft checklist for t011 releas v1 0 gate per the task s own depend list this draft depend on t001 through t006 and t010 status activ draft six of seven depend gate are met t005 remain open\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9b23eee8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"id\": \"8bf53f4b1ae56706\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3479031161753233, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18445322310760479, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7292862, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9b23eee8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1077, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:40\", \"token_count\": 704, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-07\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Blocked on Upstream PDF Library\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-26\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:10] Charlie**: Bad news on the offset mismatch fix. It's definitely coming from `pdfminer.six`. There's an open issue on their repo for the whitespace handling we're hitting.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:57] Alice**: Any workaround? We can't stay blocked on this forever.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:58] Charlie**: Leaving it blocked for now. Local patches aren't getting us a clean fix — it's too deep in the parser.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 14:18] Charlie**: Still watching upstream — there's a PR against pdfminer.six, #992, that should cover the whitespace fix, but it hasn't merged. No movement from the maintainers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 15:58] Charlie**: Spent some time this week evaluating whether we fork pdfminer.six ourselves to get the fix in sooner.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 16:01] Alice**: What's the team's read on that?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 17:55] Charlie**: We're passing on it. Maintaining a PDF parsing fork long-term is more risk than the wait. Staying blocked on #992.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:24] Charlie**: Checked again — #992 is still unmerged. No safe local path that doesn't involve owning a fork, so we're leaving the offset fix blocked pending the upstream merge.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Alice**: This is becoming a real risk for the v1.0 timeline.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Charlie**: Agreed, but I'd rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can't maintain.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 07 slack thread block on upstream pdf librari channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 26 last activ 2026 09 10 2026 06 26 09 10 charli bad news on the offset mismatch fix it s definit come from pdfminer six there s an open issu on their repo for the whitespac handl we re hit 2026 06 26 09 57 alic ani workaround we can t stay block on this forev 2026 06 26 09 58 charli leav it block for now local patch aren t get u a clean fix it s too deep in the parser 2026 08 05 14 18 charli still watch upstream there s a pr against pdfminer six 992 that should cover the whitespac fix but it hasn t merg no movement from the maintain 2026 08 20 15 58 charli spent some time this week evalu whether we fork pdfminer six ourselv to get the fix in sooner 2026 08 2016 01 alic what s the team s read on that 2026 08 2017 55 charli we re pass on it maintain a pdf pars fork long term is more risk than the wait stay block on 992 2026 09 1010 24 charli check again 992 is still unmerg no safe local path that doesn t involv own a fork so we re leav the offset fix block pend the upstream merg 2026 09 1010 41 alic this is becom a real risk for the v1 0 timelin 2026 09 1010 55 charli agre but i d rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can t maintain\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"id\": \"68389a2a4ecca69d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34588546617532334, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18445322310760479, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7225607, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1522, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:33\", \"token_count\": 462, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-60\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Async Batch Workers\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:21] Bob**: The async processing is looking good. I've integrated the progress callbacks so the GUI can show a real-time percentage.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 14:30] Diana**: I'm seeing some race conditions when two different users try to process the same file simultaneously. The lock isn't being released correctly.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:00] Bob**: Ah, I see it. I'm using the filename as the key in the lock manager, but not accounting for the user ID.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:02] Charlie**: Why not use the file hash instead? That way even if they have different filenames but it's the same content, we don't process it twice.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:12] Bob**: Good idea. I'll swap out the keys for the SHA-256 hash.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:17] Charlie**: Perfect.\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 15:35] Alice**: @Bob how does this affect the multi-threading work Charlie did?\\n\\n**[2026-08-22 16:56] Bob**: They should play well together. The scheduler distributes the *files* to different workers, and each worker uses Charlie's multi-threaded engine to process the *internal* pages.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 60 slack thread async batch worker channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 22 2026 08 22 14 21 bob the async process is look good i ve integr the progress callback so the gui can show a real time percentag 2026 08 22 14 30 diana i m see some race condit when two differ user tri to process the same file simultan the lock isn t be releas correct 2026 08 22 15 00 bob ah i see it i m use the filenam a the key in the lock manag but not account for the user id 2026 08 22 15 02 charli whi not use the file hash instead that way even if they have differ filenam but it s the same content we don t process it twice 2026 08 22 15 12 bob good idea i ll swap out the key for the sha 256 hash 2026 08 22 15 17 charli perfect 2026 08 22 15 35 alic bob how doe this affect the multi thread work charli did 2026 08 22 16 56 bob they should play well togeth the schedul distribut the file to differ worker and each worker us charli s multi thread engin to process the intern page\", \"dataset_